{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Thus says YHWH, the Elohim of Israel.</b> We do not find an explicit utterance from the Holy One, blessed be He, in this instance; even though it is not written that He, exalted be He, commanded him so, He mentioned 'the Elohim of Israel' on account of the intention of the makers of the calf, who intended to sacrifice to the Elohim of Israel. And behold, the attribute of justice struck them because they cut down the plantings, for judgment belongs to Elohim. And thus it is written of the Levites (Numbers 16:9): ״כי הבדיל אלהי ישראל אתכם מעדת ישראל״ — for the Elohim of Israel has separated you from the congregation of Israel — ״כי העבודה לאלהי ישראל״ — for the service belongs to the Elohim of Israel. So explained the Ramban, z\"l. For through the tribe of Levi the Name was sanctified publicly, just as Israel had profaned it publicly; and this is the meaning of what is written: ״ולא תחללו את שם קדשי ונקדשתי״ — and you shall not profane My holy Name, and I will be sanctified — which teaches you that the sin of profanation of YHWH is atoned by its counterpart, and that is sanctification of the Name."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {0 "The prooftext ולא תחללו את שם קדשי ונקדשתי conflates Leviticus 22:32 with the preceding verse 22:31; rendered as he quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:33.058087911Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}